-- The Sierra Peaks Section list: the peaks the catalog does not hold, and a peak-bagger's route on the
-- list peaks it holds only as climbing walls.
--
-- WHY (owner, 2026-10-21): a new tick list, with missing peaks ADDED rather than shown unreachable. The
-- roster is the Sierra Club Angeles Chapter's official list, 29th edition (2025): 247 active peaks plus
-- Pilot Knob (S), which is suspended and not added. Mount Rose is in Nevada and is filed there.
--
-- ABSENCE WAS PROVEN, NOT ASSUMED (0137's method, as in 0344): every California area read once, matched
-- by name and coordinate, then a loose probe by distinctive word within 8 km. Three list peaks were found
-- under other names (Black Kaweah, Four Gables, Bloody Mountain) and get nothing new. Six ids a new peak
-- would have taken belong to other places 3-437 km away, so those peaks carry a suffix.
--
-- WHERE A PEAK HANGS: under the parent of the nearest list peak the catalog already holds, when that is
-- within 30 km and holds no routes itself; the far north and far south of the range get two new regions;
-- Tahoe, Sonora Pass, Castle Peak and the Dinkey Lakes peaks go under the regions that already name them.
--
-- THE ROUTE: research named a route for 73 peaks, from trip reports and route descriptions read for each.
-- Where it could not confirm a name, the route is called "Standard route" and graded with the OFFICIAL
-- class, which the list defines as the class of the peak's standard route — so the row states only what
-- the list itself states. The grade is the hardest class ("2s3" is graded Class 3); a separate summit
-- block is said in the description, because a grade cell takes a value, not a sentence. Discipline
-- follows 0137: Class 1-3 scrambling, Class 4 mountaineering, Class 5 alpine. grade_num stays NULL.
--
-- Not written: trailheads, distances, gain — research disagreed too often to put numbers on the planner.
-- Re-runnable: every insert is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING. REPLAY: returns early on an empty database.

do $replay$ begin
if not exists (select 1 from areas where id = 'ca_high_sierra') then
  raise notice '0345: catalog not loaded, nothing to add'; return;
end if;

-- 1. Two containers for list peaks outside the High Sierra regions the catalog already has.
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 2. The 155 list peaks the catalog does not hold.
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 3. One route each: its confirmed name, or "Standard route" where research could not confirm one.
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 4. Walk-up sub-areas on list peaks whose climbs all sit on face sub-areas.
on conflict (id) do nothing;

-- 5. A peak-bagger's route on list peaks the catalog holds only as climbing walls.
on conflict (id) do nothing;

end $replay$;
